{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1337968-city-or-worldwide","id":1337968,"title":"City or Worldwide?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-09-26T06:29:58-07:00","id":1337968,"title":"City or Worldwide?","content":"So my group has just begun a new Mage story after about a year hiatus with yours truly as the ST (again). I often see mentioned that Mage is set as worldwide playground as opposed to a city one. Maybe it's just the way I GM/ST but I often find myself going down the path of primarily city stories.<br /> <br /> Now we do have some world travel and Umbral treks do become common during the intermediate power levels. The main focus however tends to be in a major city. The last story I ran lasted about 2 1/2 years and was based in San Francisco, this one is starting in LA (what can I say we live in Ca). <br /> <br /> How about your stories? <br /> <br /> Do you tend to stick to a single city and its surroundings or do you use an entire continent as the background?<br /> <br /> Which do you prefer, and why?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-26T06:50:56-07:00","id":1337969,"title":"","content":"My experience it's like yours. The reason for my group, I think, it's mainly because that's how we're accustomed to do it from countless times playing Vampire, and worldbuilding the whole scenario in a &quot;my city by night&quot; fashion<br /> <br /> So I can't say if I &quot;prefer&quot; this kind of things. I've played in non-WoD (D&amp;D style) stories that spaned continents, and I've liked them.<br /> <br /> I think I would like to narrate a &quot;worldwide&quot; someday, maybe. One interesting tool for worlwide (or at least larger than one city) stories it's Horizon Chantries. As these are supposed to be tied to several Nodes, it's most ordinary to think they would exist (and thus have portals) on several locations. Taking care of the Chantry's business in it's various earthly incarnations can easily give a group reasons to go arround, and thus get experience moving to locations that can easily be justified to exit on more than one city or country.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 09-26-2019, 09:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-26T10:19:30-07:00","id":1338006,"title":"","content":"I think it is going to largely depend on the party/game whether or not things go worldwide, and the plot.<br /> <br /> If the ST obviously intends for travel, there is going to involve travel. How difficult this travel is depends on how many people have correspondence 3/4 and if they have fast means of travel.<br /> <br /> I prefer whatever the ST is comfortable with, and if I'm the ST whatever the players expect, because it's real shitty to have an entire party of 'We all have abilities that work nice in this one city, someone has &quot;Phylactory&quot; set in this city, and all of our friends are in this city' then to have the ST go &quot;Congrats you are leaving the country&quot;<br /> Not to say the ST can't and shouldn't do that but expectations are important.<br /> <br /> Though personally I like adventurery-scenarios.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu","name":"Jihelu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-26T11:45:08-07:00","id":1338014,"title":"","content":"I tend to focus on local stuff at the start and gradually expand in scope and scale as the PCs grow in power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}